{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The general solution of equations of the form $\\dfrac{dy}{dt}=ky$ is\n\n$y=C\\cdot e^{kt}$\n\nfor some constant $C$.\n\nThis can be found using separation of variables. [[☃ explanation 1]]\n\nIn our case, $k=1$, so $y=C\\cdot e^{t}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{dy}{dt}\u0026=ky\n\\\\\\\\\n\\dfrac{dy}{y}\u0026=kdt\n\\\\\\\\\n\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{dy}{y}\u0026=\\displaystyle\\int kdt\n\\\\\\\\\n\\ln(|y|)\u0026=kt+c\n\\\\\\\\\ne^{\\ln(|y|)}\u0026=e^{kt+c}\n\\\\\\\\\ny\u0026=C\\cdot e^{kt}\\quad\\gray{\\text{Let }C=e^c\\geq 0}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show me how.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Let's use the fact that $y=1$ when $t=4$ to find $C$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\ny\u0026=C\\cdot e^{t}\n\\\\\\\\\n1\u0026=C\\cdot e^{4}\\quad\\gray{\\text{Plug }t=4\\text{ and }y=1}\n\\\\\\\\\ne^{-4}\u0026=C\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $y=e^{t-4}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$\\dfrac{dy}{dt}=y$, and $y=1$ when $t=4$.\n\n**Solve the equation.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$y=e^{t-4}$","correct":true},{"content":"$y=4e^{t}$","correct":false},{"content":"$y=e^{4t}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$y=4e^{t-1}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":true,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
